So, I had never ascended a Monk before. The best Monk I had previously
managed was struck down prejudicially by Kaen.

Things started out pretty okay for this guy. Began the game with the
sleep spell and found a +1 pair of jumping boots on dlvl 2 which
helped him get around pretty well in the early game. Then on dlvl 3 I
found a nice big stack of shuriken whch i kept with me for the rest of
the game (though i sort of wish i hadn't, more on that later).

Fought down to minetown, wishing a couple of times along the way that
I had started with healing instead.

The altar in minetown was glowing a comforting gray when I arrived, so
i made some holy water. And Izchak, bless his heart, sold me a cursed
magic lamp at a quite reasonable price. I don't like going down
towards Mine's End without magic resistance, so I decided to rub the
lamp immediately and was lucky enough to get the wish. Grey DSM was
out, obviously, so I considered wishing for a cloak of MR. But in the
end, i decided that that was a sucker's wish since I already had a
robe. So I wished myself up an Express Card. Clearing out Mine's end
was uneventful except that it netted me a bag of holding and a wand of
polymorph.

Retraced my steps back up to the main dungeon, stopping for a brief
sacfest, but forgetting entirely to buy protection. Sacrificing
yielded me a very welcome +5 pair of leather gloves and a moderately
welcome +5 spear (which I kept for throwing). I also recieved
Trollsbane and two different sets of +5 body armor. I shoved
Trollsbane in the BoH, though I'm not sure why. I ended up abandoning
it later having never used it. All in all, I think that the new
sacrifice mechanic is super cool. Particularly for a monk; i doubt i
would have even bothered sacrificing otherwise.

Back in the main dungeon, I had a pleasant surprise between the mines
and the oracle: a huge bookstore. I promptly murdered the shopkeeper
and then with the help of a few blessed scrolls of ID, holy water
where needed, and my wand of polymorph proceeded to learn just about
every spell in the game. In the poly spree, "megaman too" (the pony i
had tamed in the mines) got caught in the crossfire and became
destined to live out the rest of his days as a silver dragon.

Sokoban was nice enough to me to grant me an amulet of reflection. The
journey from sokoban to the castle was largely uneventful, though I
did find a pair of speed boots, a saddle and another magic lamp along
the way. I blessed the lamp in case of emergency, but decided to use
it as a light source in the interim.

Clearing out the castle was a little bit terrifying; I was still
genoless up to this point. I ended up just duking it out with a couple
of Liches and a Demilich. Fortunately, I had Repair Armour and Remove
Curse from the spellbook polyfest.

The wand was 0:1, but I had already seen scrolls of charging, i didn't
need to wish for that. I wished for a helm of brilliance, gauntlets of
dexterity and a magic marker and then enchanted everything up before
heading back to the rogue level and the magic portal thereon. It was
at this point that i broke weaponless be actually striking a monster
with my wielded stack of shurikens after enchanting them. Even though
that broke the conduct, I maintained weaponless for the rest of the
game.

Kaen fell easily this time with generous application of the sleep
spell. In the Valley of the dead a couple of wraiths dropped corpses
and I decided to break vegetarian conduct. Vlad managed to steal a
couple of levels from me, but otherwise was no great difficulty. I
swapped my amulet of refelction for the amulet of lifesaving since I
knew the reflection spell. However, it turned out that I wasn't very
good at remembering to pay attention to it wearing off and recasting
it. And so I lost my ring of free action and my ring of slow digestion
to a troll with a wand of lightning. I ended up polypiling for
replacements. After that debacle, I swapped back for the amulet of
reflection and played most of the rest of the game without the "oLS
safety net.

On my way down the the Vibrating Square, my game came very close to
ending twice.

My AC at this point was still only -12 and I was teamed up on by a
Boojum, a magical eye and a Titan at the same time. I was at 16 hit
points when i quaffed the potion of full healing.

The second time was when I found myself fighting an Arch-lich and a
Master Mind Flayer at the same time (still genoless at this point). I
thought I had it under control, but then another magical eye came onto
the scene and slow gazed me. I was able to save myself with a blessed
scroll of scare monster, a blindfold and a wand of teleportation (so
that i could fight them one at a time). At one point in there the MMF
actually got three mindsuck attacks in on me and it was only due to
sheer luck that my non-greased Helm of Brilliance blocked all three of
them.

I finally reached the bottom of gehennom and marked the VS. There were
no surprises during the trek back up to Rodney's tower. In the tower
zoo though, telepathy informed me that there was another Master Mind
Flayer and two Demiliches. "Screw this," I thought and finally wished
up a couple of scrolls of genocide.  I had found a second magic marker
as well, so i ended up going nuts and genociding 10 species in all.

Got up to the top of the tower and then ended up having to back track
all the wayback down and climb up the OUTSIDE of the tower so that I
could kill a magical eye that was making my life miserable by slow
gazing me THROUGH THE UNDIGGABLE WALLS. Once that was taken care of
dispatching Rodney was easy enough. Potion of paralysis and punches to
the face made short work of him. I performed the invocation ritual and
levelported into the sanctum. I had never done that before, but may
have to do it again in the future. I appeared three steps outside of
the sanctum. The high priest fell to a finger of death and then I
grabbed to amulet and cursed potion of gain levelled my way out of
there.

This was my first ascension run since the removal of the mysterious
force. I was really glad to see it gone. In fact, I would be happy to
even see the monster generation on the run back up cranked up a little
higher still to compensate. I ended up finally abandoning "megaman
too" at this point because i got sick of waiting for him to finish
eating at every staircase.

All in all, the ascension run was pretty easy. Rodney showed up a
couple more times but i dealt with him the same way each time.

The elemental planes were relatively painless, though i did have to
use a potion of full healing on air.

On the astral plane, I swapped out my speed boots for my boots of
jumping (still only +1) and my amulet of reflection for life saving. I
then quaffed a potion of speed and cast reflection. Even with jumping
and conflict, the Astral Plane is NOT a cakewalk at AC -15. The first
altar I went to (Death) was chaotic. I still had that blessed magic
lamp with me, but opted not to take the 50/50 chance on a Helm of
opposite alignment. Instead, I slogged my way over to the second altar
(Pestilence). I burned through 9 potions of full healing. Then ended
up actually being killed and lifesaved while fighting pestilence and
simultaneouly beaten on by angels.

There was a tense moment where i thought i was actually going to bite
it for good: I was killed by hitpoint loss, not illness. So when my
life was saved, I was still deathly ill and then Pestilence hit me
again making me feel worse. I applied my unicorn horn, but "Nothing
seem to happen."

I thought I was dead, but Pestilence missed. I took that turn to put
on my spare amulet of life saving and thankfully Pestilence didn't get
a move that turn. I applied my unicorn horn again. "What a relief!".
After that I promptly lay the beats down on him for making me scared.

Fortunately, the second altar was neutral, but the goddamned High
Priest wouldn't get out of the way, so I had to finger of death him.

Goodbye 256 the Demigod...
